{% comment %}
  Audio player, driven by _data/playlist.yml. Change track names there.

  Renders nothing when the playlist is empty. The <audio> element carries
  preload="none", so no audio is fetched until a visitor presses play, and it is a
  plain native element — no third-party embed, no ads, nothing to leak out of its
  container.

  It sits in its own fixed corner rather than in the top panel: the panel collapses
  behind the menu button on a phone, which would put the control out of reach at
  exactly the size where it is hardest to find.

  One token, which reads `[ play ]` when idle and the track name when playing.
  Tracks advance on their own, so there is nothing else to press.
{% endcomment %}

{% assign tracks = site.data.playlist %}

{% if tracks and tracks.size > 0 %}
  {% assign sources = '' | split: '' %}
  {% for track in tracks %}
    {% capture entry %}{"title":{{ track.title | jsonify }},"src":{{ track.src | relative_url | jsonify }}}{% endcapture %}
    {% assign sources = sources | push: entry %}
  {% endfor %}

  <div class="atelier-player" data-player data-player-tracks="[{{ sources | join: ',' | escape }}]">
    <button class="atelier-player__toggle" type="button" data-player-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Play">
      <span class="atelier-player__state" data-player-state>[ play ]</span>
    </button>
    <audio data-player-audio preload="none"></audio>
  </div>
{% endif %}
